description: >
  Apply when implementing or completing a defined engineering task.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Bounded task execution

Before editing:
1. read task requirements/acceptance criteria;
2. read referenced contracts/invariants;
3. inspect relevant code/tests;
4. identify expected files/areas to change;
5. identify any shared contract that would be touched.

During implementation:
- implement one bounded behaviour at a time;
- stay within scope;
- preserve state ownership and dependency direction;
- do not silently change shared contracts;
- avoid unrelated refactors;
- add tests alongside behaviour.

After implementation:
1. run focused tests;
2. run the full deterministic gate;
3. independently review the diff;
4. report deviations, assumptions, and limitations.
